# Portfolio Stack

Canonical libraries for this site. Prefer these over alternatives unless an ADR says otherwise.

## shadcn / Base UI (HARD RULE)

UI is built **on** shadcn — never invent parallel components.

1. Use `components/ui/*` when the primitive exists
2. Otherwise `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>` before writing UI
3. Feature components compose/extend those primitives; they do not replace them with hand-rolled buttons, inputs, dialogs, etc.

## Zod

- Schema source of truth for forms, tRPC inputs/outputs, and env parsing
- Infer types with `z.infer<typeof schema>` — do not duplicate hand-written interfaces

## TanStack Form

- Default form library for multi-field or validated forms
- Validate with Zod (shared schemas)
- Pair with shadcn `Field` / `Input` / `Button` when available

## nuqs

- All shareable UI state that belongs in the URL (filters, tabs, pagination, modal ids)
- Prefer typed parsers over raw `useSearchParams` string parsing

## GSAP

- Motion library for hero/section presence and intentional transitions
- Create animations in Client Components or hooks; kill/revert on cleanup (`gsap.context` or timeline `.kill()`)
- Prefer 2–3 purposeful motions per visually led page over constant decoration

## Supabase

- Persistence for portfolio **works** (and related content)
- Browser/anon client only with RLS for public reads
- Service-role client only in `server/` modules marked `server-only`
- UI never talks to Supabase directly for business reads/writes — go through tRPC

## tRPC

- Typed API between Next.js and the frontend
- Routers under `server/trpc/`; HTTP handler at `app/api/trpc/[trpc]/route.ts`
- Procedures validate with Zod; data access via `server/db/`
- Server Components may use a server-side caller; Client Components use tRPC + TanStack Query hooks

## R2 CDN (consume-only)

- Public assets via `NEXT_PUBLIC_R2_CDN_URL` and `cdnUrl()` from `@/lib/cdn`
- Configure `images.remotePatterns` in `next.config.ts` to match the CDN host
- No upload SDK in this app

